{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1767529,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"pink_un","paid":0,"title":"Designathon","festival_id":521405,"organization_id":105898,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-10T12:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-26T13:00:58+05:30","location":null,"type":"hackathons","public_url":"hackathons\/designathon-tantrafiesta26-iiitn-1767529","region":"hybrid","details":"<p>Design-A-thon is a premier <strong>UI\/UX hackathon<\/strong> that challenges participants to transform real-world problems into <strong>innovative, user-centric design solutions<\/strong>. Organized by <strong>Strokes, the official design club of IIIT Nagpur<\/strong>, this event pushes participants to explore the boundaries of creativity, problem-solving, and design methodologies under pressure.<\/p>\n<p>The competition is designed to simulate <strong>real-world design challenges<\/strong> through case studies, user research, and time-bound hackathon-style rounds. Beyond just visuals, the focus is on creating designs that are <strong>functional, inclusive, and impactful<\/strong>, delivering meaningful user experiences.<\/p>\n<p><strong>What We&rsquo;re Looking For<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams who can think creatively and craft <strong>visually stunning yet user-friendly interfaces<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Designers who can deliver <strong>seamless, intuitive, and thoughtful user journeys<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Participants ready to take on <strong>surprise challenges and constraints<\/strong>, adapting flexibly while maintaining design quality.<\/li>\n<li>Problem solvers who can balance <strong>creativity with functionality and inclusivity<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Key Details<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Design skills will be tested in <strong>realistic, case-driven environments<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Participants will work on <strong>dynamic problem statements<\/strong> with unexpected twists.<\/li>\n<li>The goal is to inspire creativity while grounding designs in <strong>practical usability and accessibility<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Structure<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Round 1 &ndash; Online Case Study Submission<\/p>\n<p>Participants will undertake a <strong>research-driven design project<\/strong>, such as:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Creating <strong>user personas<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Conducting <strong>heuristic evaluations<\/strong> of popular designs<\/li>\n<li>Critiquing design flaws in major platforms\/projects<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Each case study submission must include:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Research findings with <strong>insights and data<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Clear identification of <strong>UX issues and pain points<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Practical recommendations for <strong>design improvements<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Mockups, wireframes, or prototypes<\/strong> showcasing solutions<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>One comprehensive <strong>PDF case study<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Supporting visuals (PNG\/JPEG\/PDF)<\/li>\n<li>Optional: Video explanation of design process<\/li>\n<li>Optional: Figma or source files as supplementary material<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Timeline:<\/strong> 10th oct, 12:00 AM &ndash; 19 Oct, 11:59 PM<\/p>\n<p>Round 2 &ndash; Offline Finals (16-Hour Hackathon)<\/p>\n<p>A <strong>16-hour on-campus design hackathon<\/strong> where teams receive the problem statement at the start. They must research, ideate, and deliver a <strong>complete design solution<\/strong> within the deadline.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Key Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables include <strong>wireframes, prototypes, and final designs<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Teams may use any <strong>design tools or collaboration platforms<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>Judging criteria: Functionality, creativity, user experience, aesthetics, adaptability<\/li>\n<li>Surprise twists may include <strong>target audience shifts, theme reversals, limited palettes, or mandatory design elements<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Timeline:<\/strong> 25th Oct, 9:00 PM &ndash; 26th Oct, 3:00 PM<\/p>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Criteria<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Case Study<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Research depth &amp; clarity<\/li>\n<li>Identification of design flaws<\/li>\n<li>Feasibility of recommendations<\/li>\n<li>Quality of supporting prototypes<\/li>\n<li>Professional presentation<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &ndash; Offline Finals<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Creativity &amp; innovation of design<\/li>\n<li>Usability &amp; functionality<\/li>\n<li>Adherence to problem statement<\/li>\n<li>Visual &amp; aesthetic quality<\/li>\n<li>Adaptability to restrictions<\/li>\n<li>Presentation clarity<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to <strong>all students across India<\/strong> (any discipline)<\/li>\n<li>Teams of <strong>2&ndash;4 members<\/strong>, or individuals allowed<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college &amp; cross-specialization teams welcome<\/li>\n<li>Each participant can only join <strong>one team<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Requirements (Final Round)<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>Figma design file link<\/strong> containing:\n<ul>\n<li>Research insights<\/li>\n<li>Wireframes<\/li>\n<li>Prototypes<\/li>\n<li>Final design<\/li>\n<li>Dedicated <strong>presentation section<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>File must be set to &ldquo;anyone with the link can view&rdquo;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>General Rules &amp; Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All submissions must be <strong>original work<\/strong> (strict no-plagiarism policy)<\/li>\n<li>Participants must bring their own laptops\/equipment for offline rounds<\/li>\n<li>Respect IIITN&rsquo;s campus rules and code of conduct<\/li>\n<li>Organizers&rsquo; and judges&rsquo; decisions are <strong>final.<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":2087901,"moderation